    FONTMAN and PALMAN are tools for easy design of custom character fonts
    and color palettes in text mode. VGA adapter card is required.

    The VGA.COM utility activates character fonts or color palettes from
    a file - on the command line or in BAT files.

    DEMO.BAT will give you an impression of what you can do with these
    tools (ANSI device driver not required).

    For more details see DOC files.

    Note:
    FONTMAN will also work with a 400 by 640 LCD VGA display, but the
    sample fonts in this package take advantage of the full 400 by 720
    CRT screen resolution (with an extra space between characters).

    For your information:
    These programs only use documented BIOS and DOS calls - no direct
    access to controller ports.

    --------------- Files of the FONTMAN+PALMAN package -----------------

    DEMO.BAT, .AN1..5   DEMO,  ANSI files (displayed with VTYPE)

    FONTMAN.COM, .DOC   character font editor
    PALMAN.COM, .DOC    color palette editor
    VGA.COM, .DOC       utility to activate fonts, palettes & more
    VTYPE.COM, DOC      fast TYPE replacement with ANSI emulation
    XVRESET.COM, DOC    TSR, catches unnecessary video resets

                        character fonts:
    DONNA.FNT
    FLORI.FNT
    MINI.F08            for 50 text lines
    ORATOR.FNT
    SANSERIF.FNT
    SANSF1.FNT          with special frame characters (see DEMO.AN3)
    SANSMALL.F12        SanSerif, for 33 text lines

                        color palettes:
    MY.PAL
    PALE.PAL
    STANDARD.PAL        copied from VGA card

    TEST.FLD            test patterns for FONTMAN (sample file)
    READ.ME             this file

